    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Restore fonts-stix in the Debian install command for MathML fonts]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45337</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45337"/>
        <updated>2026-08-27T17:16:40.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198354403?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">I restored <code class="notranslate">fonts-stix</code> to the Debian install command and removed the note saying that package ships STIX 1.x. This reverts the change made in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4611786815" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44385" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/44385/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44385">#44385</a>.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">The current maintainer of Debian's <code class="notranslate">fonts-stix</code> package reported in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5213629439" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45274" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/45274/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45274">#45274</a> that they took the package over and upgraded it to STIX Two, so the original command works again.</p>
<p dir="auto">I checked the archive before making the change:</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role="table">
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Release</th>
<th><code class="notranslate">fonts-stix</code> version</th>
<th>Math font it installs</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Debian testing (forky) and unstable (sid)</td>
<td>2.13b171+ds-2</td>
<td><code class="notranslate">STIXTwoMath-Regular.otf</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Debian 13 (stable)</td>
<td>1.1.1-5</td>
<td><code class="notranslate">STIXMath-Regular.otf</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Ubuntu 26.04 and later</td>
<td>2.13b171+ds-2</td>
<td><code class="notranslate">STIXTwoMath-Regular.otf</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Ubuntu 24.04</td>
<td>1.1.1-5</td>
<td><code class="notranslate">STIXMath-Regular.otf</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir="auto">Version 2.13b171 is the same release that the Windows and macOS instructions on this page already link to, so readers on those releases now get the exact font the page asks them to install.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto">There is a tradeoff here that I want to flag for reviewers rather than bury. On Debian 13 and Ubuntu 24.04 the command still pulls STIX 1.x, and this PR removes the note that warned about that. Those releases are what most readers are running today, and warning about them is why <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4611786815" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44385" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/44385/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44385">#44385</a> was filed in the first place.</p>
<p dir="auto">I went with the straight revert because the issue asks for it and <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/Josh-Cena/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/Josh-Cena">@Josh-Cena</a> said in the issue that reverting was fine. If you would rather keep a warning for the older releases, I can scope the advice by release instead: leave <code class="notranslate">fonts-lmodern</code> on its own, then add a second <code class="notranslate">fonts-stix</code> command noted as applying to Debian testing and unstable and to Ubuntu 26.04 and later. I have that version ready and can swap it in, so let me know which you prefer.</p>
<p dir="auto">Sources I used:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://api.ftp-master.debian.org/madison?package=fonts-stix" rel="nofollow">Debian madison for <code class="notranslate">fonts-stix</code></a></li>
<li><a href="https://packages.debian.org/sid/all/fonts-stix/filelist" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">fonts-stix</code> file list in sid</a></li>
<li><a href="https://packages.debian.org/trixie/all/fonts-stix/filelist" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">fonts-stix</code> file list in trixie</a></li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #45274.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5213629439" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45274" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/45274/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45274">#45274</a><br>
Relates to <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4611786815" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44385" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/44385/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44385">#44385</a><br>
Relates to <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2842949371" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/38089" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/38089/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/38089">#38089</a></p>]]></content>
